          }
        ],
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "md",
            "md": "## Allocation"
          },
          {
            "t": "database",
            "db": "targets",
            "view": "all"
          },
          {
            "t": "md",
            "md": "## Plan"
          },
          {
            "t": "pageLink",
            "page": "ips"
          },
          {
            "t": "pageLink",
            "page": "rebalance"
          },
          {
            "t": "pageLink",
            "page": "review"
          },
          {
            "t": "md",
            "md": "## Holdings"
          },
          {
            "t": "database",
            "db": "holdings"
          },
          {
            "t": "database",
            "db": "securities",
            "view": "all"
          },
          {
            "t": "disclaimer"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ips",
      "kind": "page",
      "optional": false,
      "spec": {
        "title": "Investment Policy Statement",
        "icon": "📜",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "callout",
            "icon": "🧭",
            "color": "blue",
            "md": "An IPS is a one-page promise to your future self. Write it while markets are calm; read it when they are not."
          },
          {
            "t": "md",
            "md": "## Goal\n**{{if(answers.risk_goal == \"\", \"Long-term growth\", answers.risk_goal)}}** over a horizon of **{{if(answers.risk_horizon == \"gt10\", \"more than 10 years\", if(answers.risk_horizon == \"lt3\", \"under 3 years\", \"3–10 years\"))}}**.\n\n## Target allocation\nPreset: **{{answers.targets_preset}}** — an example starting point, not a recommendation. The targets live in the Target allocation table below and must add up to 100%.\n\n## Rebalancing\n- Method: **{{answers.rebalance_mode}}**, checked **{{answers.rebalance_calendar}}**.\n- Bands: rebalance a class when it drifts more than **{{answers.rebalance_bandabs}} percentage points** or **{{answers.rebalance_bandrel}}% of its target** away.\n- New money first: direct contributions to the most underweight class before selling anything.\n- Avoid selling in taxable accounts when a tax-advantaged account can do the job.\n\n## Rules I follow when markets fall\n1. I do not sell because prices dropped; I check my bands instead.\n2. I keep my emergency fund outside the portfolio so I am never a forced seller.\n3. I keep contributing on schedule — lower prices buy more shares.\n4. I wait 48 hours before any change that is not in this document.\n5. I review this statement once a year, not after every headline.\n\n## Costs\nPrefer low-cost, diversified funds. An expense ratio above 0.5% is flagged by the advisor.\n\n---\nSigned: ____________________   Date: ____________"
          },
          {
            "t": "database",
            "db": "targets",
            "view": "all"
          },
          {
            "t": "disclaimer"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "rebalance",
      "kind": "page",
      "optional": false,
      "spec": {
        "title": "Rebalance planner",
        "icon": "⚖️",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "md",
            "md": "## How rebalancing bands work\nEach asset class has a **target** and two bands. A class is *outside its band* when its drift (current % − target %) is more than:\n- the **absolute band** — {{answers.rebalance_bandabs}} percentage points, or\n- the **relative band** — {{answers.rebalance_bandrel}}% of the target (for a 20% target, 5 points).\n\nThis \"5/25\" rule is a common guideline: small drifts are left alone, which keeps trading and taxes low.\n\n## Steps, in order\n1. **New cash first.** Put contributions and dividends into the most underweight classes.\n2. **Tax-advantaged accounts next.** Trades inside IRAs and 401(k)s do not create taxable gains.\n3. **Taxable sells last**, and only if you allow them: losses first, then the highest-basis lots.\n4. Skip trades smaller than **{{fmt_money(coalesce(answers.rebalance_mintrade, 50))}}**.\n\nEMP suggests trades; it never places them."
          },
          {
            "t": "database",
            "db": "targets",
            "view": "all"
          },
          {
            "t": "disclaimer"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "review",
      "kind": "page",
      "optional": false,
      "spec": {
        "title": "Annual investing review",
        "icon": "🔎",
        "template": true,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "t": "checklist",
            "items": [
              "Re-read the Investment Policy Statement",
              "Check allocation against targets and bands",
              "Review fees and expense ratios",
              "Confirm contributions (employer match, IRA, HSA limits)",
              "Look for tax-loss harvesting opportunities in taxable accounts",
              "Update beneficiaries",
              "Sign and date the IPS again"
            ]
          },
          {
            "t": "disclaimer"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
